  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>UVDelta 06 isn't your typical local clinic: it's a structure entirely dedicated to veterinary emergencies in the Alpes-Maritimes, based in Saint-Laurent-du-Var. There are no routine consultations or courtesy vaccinations here: the team is organised to handle emergencies, resuscitation and intensive care for animals, including outside the opening hours of regular clinics.</p>

      <div class="callout" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><svg><use href="#i-alert"/></svg> UVDelta 06's official website presents itself as a clinic dedicated to emergencies, open 24/7 on nights, weekends and public holidays, with home or in-clinic visits possible. The vet directories and social networks that repeat this description merely copy this same original statement, which does not make it an independent confirmation.</div>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>UVDelta 06 takes over from the department's regular vet clinics when they're closed: at night, on weekends and on public holidays. If your dog has a health issue during these times during your stay in the Alpes-Maritimes, this is the kind of structure to contact first, alongside your regular vet, who can also point you in the right direction.</p>
      <p>The phone number (0 800 94 84 84) is a free number dedicated to emergencies: call before heading over, the team can assess the situation and tell you what to do next. Targeted search for any negative signals (emergencies not actually handled, unreachable phone line): none found — positive reviews ("top team", "very professional").</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Saint-Laurent-du-Var is a coastal town, between Nice and Cagnes-sur-Mer, easily reachable from most towns in the department in case of urgent need.</p>
